Create an EIGHT FRAME WALK CYCLE sprite sheet of this exact tuxedo cat. Reference is character identity, NOT pose. Cat is now on all FOUR legs in perfectly consistent LEFT FACING SIDE VIEW in every frame. Preserve charcoal coat, ivory chest and muzzle, white socks, amber eyes, tall ears and white-tipped long tail. Opaque pixel clusters on genuinely transparent background. Flat restrained palette, crisp pixel edges, no background, glow, text, labels or shadows.
Layout EXACTLY 4 columns x 2 rows, 8 equally sized cells on a 2:1 landscape canvas. Entire cat contained in each cell with 15 percent padding, same scale, head position, torso length and feet baseline. NO seated poses. Each frame is the next eighth of one slow natural quadruped walk cycle, read left to right then second row. Animate near and far legs as separate limbs, far legs darker:
1 near foreleg reaches forward contacting floor, near hindleg behind;
2 near foreleg begins pushing back under body, far hindleg lifts;
3 near foreleg underneath shoulder, near hindleg swings forward;
4 near foreleg back, near hindleg lands forward, far foreleg forward;
5 opposite contact: near foreleg fully back starting lift, far foreleg fully forward planted, near hindleg forward;
6 near foreleg lifted curling forward, far foreleg pushes backward;
7 near foreleg passing forward off floor, near hindleg pushes back;
8 near foreleg reaching toward first contact, transitions seamlessly to frame 1.
Head and torso stay almost unchanged, maximum ONE logical pixel vertical bob. Tail is a shallow upward curve behind cat with subtle tip flex, never changes shape wildly. Exactly four legs, no duplicated paws, no running or jumping. Distinct leg positions, credible feline joint bending. This is an actual sequential animation sprite sheet, not a pose exploration.
